    'Pomogni suradniku oko „Vježbaj odgovor na „Je li ovo za mene?”” kao da zajedno prolazite njegov dan. Situacija primjera: Odgovor zainteresiranoj osobi koja nije sigurna odgovara li joj posao. Primjer tona: „Razumijem što misliš. Ajmo prvo proći što bi radila i koliko ti vremena odgovara odvojiti. Onda ćeš puno lakše vidjeti je li to nešto za tebe, bez žurbe da odmah odlučiš.” Preuzmi toplinu i način govora, ali ne tuđu priču. Ako suradnik potvrdi vlastito korištenje i zadovoljstvo, sačuvaj to iskustvo u njegovoj poruci. Bez te potvrde ne dodaj iskustvo ni oduševljenje. Upute zadrži izvan same poruke. Za završetak i dalje vrijedi: Imaš realan odgovor i završetak razgovora, bez jamstva uspjeha ili pritiska.' => 'Help the member with “Practice answering ‘Is this right for me?’” as though you are going through their day together. Example situation: Responding to an interested person who is unsure whether the business is right for her. Example tone: “I understand what you mean. Let\'s first go over what you would do and how much time you\'d be comfortable setting aside. Then it\'ll be much easier for you to see whether it\'s right for you, without rushing to decide now.” Take the warmth and conversational style, but not someone else\'s story. If the member confirms that they have used the product themselves and are satisfied, keep that experience in their message. Without that confirmation, do not add any experience or enthusiasm. Keep instructions out of the message itself. The completion criterion still applies: You have a realistic answer and a way to end the conversation, without a guarantee of success or pressure.',
