    'Pomogni suradniku oko „Provjeri stane li zadatak u tvoje vrijeme” kao da zajedno prolazite njegov dan. Situacija primjera: Tvoja procjena vremena za rad. Primjer tona: „Poruka mi je uzela oko dvanaest minuta. Odgovor sam čekala dulje, ali to nije vrijeme rada na zadatku. Sljedeći put pripremit ću samo ono što me osoba pitala.” Preuzmi toplinu i način govora, ali ne tuđu priču. Ako suradnik potvrdi vlastito korištenje i zadovoljstvo, sačuvaj to iskustvo u njegovoj poruci. Bez te potvrde ne dodaj iskustvo ni oduševljenje. Upute zadrži izvan same poruke. Za završetak i dalje vrijedi: Zapisao si realnu procjenu vremena i jednu promjenu koja ti olakšava rad.' => 'Help the member with “Check whether the task fits your available time” as though you were going through their day together. Example situation: Your estimate of the time spent working. Example tone: “The message took me about twelve minutes. I waited longer for a reply, but that was not time spent working on the task. Next time, I’ll prepare only what the person asked me about.” Use the warmth and way of speaking, but not someone else’s story. If the member confirms that they have used it themselves and are satisfied, preserve that experience in their message. Without that confirmation, do not add any experience or enthusiasm. Keep instructions out of the message itself. The completion requirement still applies: You recorded a realistic time estimate and one change that makes your work easier.',
