    'Pomogni suradniku oko „Javi se suradniku koji je zapeo” kao da zajedno prolazite njegov dan. Situacija primjera: Suradniku s kojim već imaš dogovorenu podršku. Primjer tona: „Ej [ime], kako si, kako ti ide? Ako si na nečemu zapela, javi pa ćemo proći zajedno. A ako ti je ovih dana gužva, i to je u redu — dogovorit ćemo kad ti odgovara.” Preuzmi toplinu i način govora, ali ne tuđu priču. Ako suradnik potvrdi vlastito korištenje i zadovoljstvo, sačuvaj to iskustvo u njegovoj poruci. Bez te potvrde ne dodaj iskustvo ni oduševljenje. Upute zadrži izvan same poruke. Za završetak i dalje vrijedi: Poslao si primjereno pitanje ili napravio jasno označenu vježbu podrške.' => 'Help the member with “Check in with a member who\'s stuck” as though you were going through their day together. Example situation: A member you\'ve already agreed to support. Example tone: “Hey [ime], how are you? How\'s it going? If you\'re stuck on anything, let me know and we can go through it together. And if you\'re busy at the moment, that\'s fine too. We can arrange a time that works for you.” Keep the warmth and way of speaking, but not someone else\'s story. If the member confirms their own use and satisfaction, preserve that experience in their message. Without that confirmation, do not add experience or enthusiasm. Keep instructions outside the message itself. The completion requirement still applies: You sent an appropriate question or completed a clearly labelled support exercise.',
