    'Primjer: novim suradnicima koji tek kreću, ljudima koji žele preporuku proizvoda ili partnerima koji grade posao uz postojeći posao.' => 'Example: new collaborators, people looking for product guidance, or partners building the business alongside another job.',
    '30 popusta' => '30 discounts',
    'Nedavne coaching aktivnosti' => 'Recent coaching activity',
    'Pomogni suradniku oko „Predstavi posao bez naučenog govora” kao da zajedno prolazite njegov dan. Situacija primjera: Osobi koja želi razumjeti posao, uz zaseban prolazak provjerenih uvjeta. Primjer tona: „Baš bih ti voljela pokazati kako mi izgleda rad s Foreverom, da ne ostane sve na pričanju. Proći ćemo i vrijeme, troškove i uvjete — zarada nije zagarantirana. Onda u miru procijeniš vidiš li sebe u tome.” Preuzmi toplinu i način govora, ali ne tuđu priču. Ako suradnik potvrdi vlastito korištenje i zadovoljstvo, sačuvaj to iskustvo u njegovoj poruci. Bez te potvrde ne dodaj iskustvo ni oduševljenje. Upute zadrži izvan same poruke. Za završetak i dalje vrijedi: Imaš cjelovito, razumljivo objašnjenje bez obećavanja prihoda i prešućivanja obveza.' => 'Help the member with “Present the business without a rehearsed speech” as if you were going through their day together. Example situation: Speaking to someone who wants to understand the business, with a separate review of verified terms. Example tone: “I’d really like to show you what working with Forever looks like for me, rather than just talking about it. We’ll also go through the time, costs and terms. Earnings are not guaranteed. Then you can decide at your own pace whether you can see yourself doing it.” Use the warmth and way of speaking, but not someone else’s story. If the member confirms their own use and satisfaction, keep that experience in their message. Without that confirmation, do not add experience or enthusiasm. Keep instructions out of the message itself. The completion requirement still applies: You have a complete, understandable explanation that does not promise income or leave out obligations.',
