    'Pomogni suradniku oko „Provjeri kome se i kada trebaš javiti” kao da zajedno prolazite njegov dan. Situacija primjera: Bilješka uz kontakt, ne tekst koji šalješ kupcu. Primjer tona: „Zanimaju je proizvodi, o poslu zasad ne želi pričati. Rekla je da joj petak odgovara pa ću se tada javiti.” Preuzmi toplinu i način govora, ali ne tuđu priču. Ako suradnik potvrdi vlastito korištenje i zadovoljstvo, sačuvaj to iskustvo u njegovoj poruci. Bez te potvrde ne dodaj iskustvo ni oduševljenje. Upute zadrži izvan same poruke. Za završetak i dalje vrijedi: Provjerio si barem jedan kontakt ili pripremio primjer bilješke ako još nemaš kontakata.' => 'Help the member with “Check who you need to contact and when” as if you were going through their day together. Example situation: A note attached to a contact, not text you send to a customer. Example tone: “She is interested in the products, but does not want to talk about the business for now. She said Friday works for her, so I will get in touch then.” Use the warmth and conversational style, but not someone else\'s story. If the member confirms that they have used the product and are happy with it, keep that experience in their message. Without that confirmation, do not add experience or enthusiasm. Keep instructions out of the message itself. The completion requirement still applies: You have checked at least one contact or prepared a sample note if you do not have any contacts yet.',
