    'Pomogni suradniku oko „Provjeri treba li kupcu pojašnjenje” kao da zajedno prolazite njegov dan. Situacija primjera: Dogovoreno javljanje kupcu koji je već dobio proizvod. Primjer tona: „Bok [ime], kako ti ide s [proizvod]? Jesi se snašla s korištenjem? Ako te nešto buni, piši mi pa ćemo to zajedno proći.” Preuzmi toplinu i način govora, ali ne tuđu priču. Ako suradnik potvrdi vlastito korištenje i zadovoljstvo, sačuvaj to iskustvo u njegovoj poruci. Bez te potvrde ne dodaj iskustvo ni oduševljenje. Upute zadrži izvan same poruke. Za završetak i dalje vrijedi: Javio si se prema dogovoru. Odgovor i daljnju pomoć upiši samo ako ih je stvarno bilo.' => 'Help the member with “Check whether the customer needs clarification” as if you were going through their day together. Example situation: An agreed follow up with a customer who has already received the product. Example tone: “Hi [ime], how are you getting on with [proizvod]? Have you figured out how to use it? If anything is confusing, message me and we\'ll go through it together.” Keep the warmth and way of speaking, but don\'t borrow someone else\'s story. If the member confirms they have used it themselves and are happy with it, keep that experience in their message. Without that confirmation, don\'t add experience or enthusiasm. Keep instructions outside the message itself. The completion requirement still applies: You followed up as agreed. Record a reply and any further help only if they actually happened.',
