    'Pomogni suradniku oko „Razjasni što osoba pokušava odabrati” kao da zajedno prolazite njegov dan. Situacija primjera: Nakon što osoba sama kaže da želi jednostavnije korištenje. Primjer tona: „Samo da te dobro razumijem — htjela bi manje koraka ili ti je važnije da se proizvod lakše koristi? Pitam da ti pokažem ono što ti stvarno odgovara.” Preuzmi toplinu i način govora, ali ne tuđu priču. Ako suradnik potvrdi vlastito korištenje i zadovoljstvo, sačuvaj to iskustvo u njegovoj poruci. Bez te potvrde ne dodaj iskustvo ni oduševljenje. Upute zadrži izvan same poruke. Za završetak i dalje vrijedi: Sažeo si pitanje osobe i pripremio ili poslao jedno potrebno potpitanje.' => 'Help the member with “Clarify what the person is trying to choose” as if you were going through their day together. Example situation: After the person says they want something simpler to use. Example tone: “Just so I understand you correctly, would you like fewer steps, or is it more important that the product is easier to use? I\'m asking so I can show you what really suits you.” Use the warmth and way of speaking, but not someone else\'s story. If the member confirms that they have used the product themselves and are happy with it, keep that experience in their message. Without that confirmation, do not add personal experience or enthusiasm. Keep instructions out of the message itself. The completion requirement still applies: You have summarised the person\'s question and prepared or sent one necessary follow up question.',
